    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to assign a `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is derived purely from the owner's own fields (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`) and is a read-only output, I followed the existing precedent for the derived `displayName`/`initials` fields \u2014 computed in the MapStruct mapper rather than stored on the entity:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   The `%02d` ensures pre-2010 years zero-pad correctly (e.g. 2005 \u2192 `05`), matching the test's `substring(2, 4)` extraction.\n\nThis works for both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads, since `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are persisted on the entity at creation time.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
